            "explanation": "The answer is 22.5°\nWhen the minute hand is pointing to the 9 [indicating 45 minutes past the hour], the hour hand will have moved three-quarters of the angle between the 9 and the 10 on the clock dial. The angle between the 9 and the 10 is 30 degrees so the hour hand will have moved three-quarters of 30 degrees, or 22.5 degrees. The angle between the hands is, therefore, 22.5 degrees.",
