            "explanation": "The answer is\nProb of scoring 12  =  (Prob of scoring 6 on fair dice)  ×  (Prob of scoring 6 on biased dice)\nAs the question tells us that the Prob of scoring 12 is\nCombining the above two statements, we can write:\nx (Prob of scoring 6 on biased dice)  =\nRearranging this gives:\n(Prob of scoring 6 on biased dice) =\nAs the probability of scoring a 1 or 2 or 3 or 4 or 5 is the same on the biased dice, we can deduce that:\n(Prob of scoring 1 on the biased dice) =\nAnd so this gives:\nProb of scoring 2 = (Prob of scoring 1 on fair dice) × (Prob of scoring 1 on biased dice)\nor\nProb of scoring 2 is",
